{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Smite the loins of those who rise against him.</b> He smites his adversaries with a blow to the loins, in the sense of what is said (Psalms 69) ״וּמָתְנֵיהֶם תָּמִיד הַמְעַד״ — and he said this concerning those who stir up against the priesthood. Another interpretation: He saw that the Hasmonean and his sons were destined to wage war against the Greeks, and he prayed on their behalf, because they were few — twelve sons of the Hasmonean and Elazar — against many myriads; therefore it is said <b>Bless, O YHWH, his substance, and accept the work of his hands</b> (Bereshit Rabbah 99):" "<b>and may those who hate Him not rise.</b> Smite his adversaries and his haters from having any resurgence."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:42.988238713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}